{"packet_id":"D079-01","doc_id":"D079","jurisdiction":"San Francisco, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"San Francisco Rent Ordinance just cause eviction requirement","requirement":"A landlord may evict a tenant from a unit covered by the Rent Ordinance only for one of the 17 just cause reasons in Section 37.9(a); the mere expiration of a rental agreement or a change in ownership is not just cause.","key_value":"17 just cause reasons","coverage_conditions":"Rental units covered by the Rent Ordinance, including tenancies exempt from its rent increase limits such as units first obtaining a Certificate of Occupancy after June 13, 1979, Costa-Hawkins tenancies, and some tenancies rent-regulated by another agency.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Units covered by the Rent Ordinance, including those exempt from rent increase limits"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"A landlord who evicts or tries to evict a tenant unlawfully may be subject to substantial civil and/or criminal liability.","effective_date":null,"citation":"S.F. Admin. Code § 37.9(a)","quoted_span":"In order to evict a tenant from a rental unit covered by the Rent Ordinance, a landlord must have a \"just cause\" reason that is the dominant motive for pursuing the eviction. Note that the mere expiration of a rental agreement or a change in ownership does not constitute \"just cause\" for eviction.","interaction":"Tenancies exempt from the Ordinance's rent increase limitations remain subject to its eviction provisions.","confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D079-01","doc_id":"D079","jurisdiction":"San Francisco, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Just cause required to remove housing services","requirement":"A landlord needs a just cause reason to take away or remove access to housing services such as garage, parking, driveway, storage and laundry facilities, though parking and storage may be temporarily removed for mandatory soft-story seismic retrofit work.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Tenants in rental units covered by the Rent Ordinance; temporary removal of parking and storage spaces is allowed where the landlord complies with Ordinance Section 37.2(r) for mandatory soft-story seismic retrofit work.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Units covered by the Rent Ordinance"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Overview of Just Cause Evictions, SF.gov (Rent Board)","quoted_span":"The landlord also needs a \"just cause“ reason to take away or remove access to certain housing services, including but not limited to garage facilities, parking facilities, driveways, storage spaces, and laundry rooms.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
